  "identifier": "frieren-s2-announce-2026",
  "headline": "Frieren: Beyond Journey's End season 2 confirmed, Golden Land arc to air in winter 2026",
  "description": "Season 2 of the TV anime Frieren: Beyond Journey's End has been officially announced. The new season will adapt the Golden Land (Aureole) arc that follows the First-Class Mage Exam and explores Frieren's past and the fate of souls.",
  "articleBody": "Shogakukan and Madhouse announced on February 13 that a second season of the TV anime Frieren: Beyond Journey's End is in production. The broadcast is planned for the winter 2026 cour, focusing on the Golden Land (Aureole) arc from the original manga.\n\nSeason 1 aired in fall 2023 and drew attention for debuting with a two-hour Friday Roadshow special. Its detailed animation and delicate emotional storytelling earned strong domestic and international praise and a sweep of multiple anime awards.\n\nThe Golden Land arc follows Frieren and her party as they travel toward Aureole, the land said to hold the souls of the dead. The storyline revisits her memories of Himmel while pursuing the truth about a place where the living can meet the dead, reinforcing the series' themes of time and loss.\n\nKey staff are returning from season 1, including director Keiichiro Saito and series composition writer Tomohiro Suzuki, with Madhouse maintaining production quality.\n\nOriginal author Kanehito Yamada said he is happy to see an arc that touches the core of Frieren's journey animated, raising expectations for how season 2 will deepen the carefully built narrative.",
  "articleSection": "anime-news",
